No TypeScript type augmentation is provided for the `toHaveLiveRegion` custom matcher. Consumers who follow the documented usage of `expect.extend({ toHaveLiveRegion })` will get a TypeScript error (`Property 'toHaveLiveRegion' does not exist on type 'Assertion'`) since the Vitest types don't know about this matcher. The codebase already has a precedent for `declare module` augmentation in `code/core/src/test/index.ts`. A companion declaration should be co-located with `toHaveLiveRegion.ts` or in its own `.d.ts`, e.g.:

```ts
declare module 'vitest' {
  interface Assertion<R = any> {
    toHaveLiveRegion(options: LiveRegionMatcherOptions): R;
  }
  interface AsymmetricMatchersContaining {
    toHaveLiveRegion(options: LiveRegionMatcherOptions): any;
  }
}
```
